Here is the study in JSON format with logical operators:

```
{
    "IC": [
        {
            "IC1": "Women 18 to 40 years of age inclusive who can give written informed consent"
        },
        {
            "IC2": "Available for all visits and consent to follow all procedures scheduled for the study"
        },
        {
            "IC3": "Agree to daily application of gel and monitoring as per Daily Monitored Adherence (DMA) method"
        },
        {
            "IC4": "Healthy and self-reported sexually active"
        },
        {
            "IC5": "HIV-negative as determined by a HIV rapid test at time of enrollment"
        },
        {
            "IC6": "On a stable form of contraception and willing to continue on this stable method of contraception, OR, Have undergone surgical sterilisation at least 3 months prior to enrollment"
        },
        {
            "IC7": "In the absence of the use of exogenous hormone(s), have a self-reported regular menstrual cycle defined as having a minimum of 21 days and a maximum of 36 days between menses"
        },
        {
            "IC8": "Upon pelvic/speculum examination and colposcopy at the time of enrollment, the cervix and vagina appear normal as determined by the investigator"
        },
        {
            "IC9": "Asymptomatic for genital infections at the time of enrollment"
        },
        {
            "IC10": "Willing to refrain from use of vaginal products or objects within 14 days prior to enrollment and for the duration of the study"
        },
        {
            "IC11": "Willing to answer acceptability and adherence questionnaires throughout the study"
        },
        {
            "IC12": "Willing to refrain from participation in any other research study for the duration of this study"
        },
        {
            "IC13": "Willing to provide adequate locator information for study retention purposes and be reachable per local standard procedures"
        }
    ],
    "EC": [
        {
            "EC1": "Currently pregnant or last pregnancy outcome within 3 months prior to enrolment"
        },
        {
            "EC2": "Currently breast-feeding"
        },
        {
            "EC3": "Participated in any other research study within 60 days prior to screening"
        },
        {
            "EC4": "Previously participated in any HIV vaccine study"
        },
        {
            "EC5": "Untreated urogenital infections (either symptomatic or asymptomatic) within 2 weeks prior to enrollment"
        },
        {
            "EC6": "Presence of abnormal physical finding on the vulva, vaginal walls or cervix during pelvic/speculum examination and/or colposcopy"
        },
        {
            "EC7": "History of significant urogenital or uterine prolapse, undiagnosed vaginal bleeding, urethral obstruction"
        },
        {
            "EC8": "Pap smear result at screening that requires cryotherapy, biopsy, treatment (other than for infection), or further evaluation"
        },
        {
            "EC9": "Any Grade 2, 3 or 4 baseline haematology, chemistry or urinalysis laboratory abnormality according to the DAIDS Table for Grading Adverse Experiences"
        },
        {
            "EC10": "Unexplained, undiagnosed abnormal bleeding per vagina, bleeding per vagina during or following vaginal intercourse, or gynaecologic surgery within 90 days prior to enrollment"
        },
        {
            "EC11": "Any history of anaphylaxis or severe allergy resulting in angioedema; or a history of sensitivity/allergy to latex"
        },
        {
            "EC12": "Any serious acute, chronic or progressive disease"
        },
        {
            "EC13": "Any condition(s) that, in the opinion of the investigator, might interfere with adherence to study requirements or evaluation of the study objectives"
        }
    ]
}
```

Note: I used the same format as before, with each inclusion criterion (IC) or exclusion criterion (EC) represented as a separate object with a single key-value pair. The value is the text of the criterion.